body:
Including `jsonString` in the dependency array causes the effect to run on every keystroke, which defeats the purpose of the comparison logic. The effect should only synchronize when `value` changes externally, not when the user types (which updates `jsonString` via `handleChange`).

Remove `jsonString` from the dependency array on line 42. The effect only needs `value` as a dependency. This will prevent unnecessary re-runs and potential issues when the user is typing invalid JSON.
```suggestion
  }, [value]);
```
